From a847f07cb792ae9897181cd9e9cb6c1be8f77588 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: root <root@MSI.localdomain>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 22:56:43 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] runtime: padded targets render in place only where the
 driver's stores stay in their rows

PaddedTargetsPolicy::Alias (0003) renders a padded texture over a buffer
in place, an image over the buffer's rows at Metal's pitch. On Turnip that
image's GMEM stores do not stop at the texture's last texel: where a render
area ends at the image's right or bottom edge, tu_attachment_store_unaligned
lets the store run on to the next multiple of gmem_align_w x gmem_align_h
(16 x 4 texels on Adreno 6xx to 8xx, A6xxGPUInfo), "since it will write
into padding space"; a single-level linear image takes no y2 alignment
(fd6_view.cc's need_y2_align). On the phone a 1125 x 64 RGBA8 surface at
4608-byte rows rendered in place had 44 bytes after each row's 4500 changed
(1125 texels written as 1136). With rows narrower than the aligned width
those writes reach the next row's first texels, and below a height that is
not a multiple of 4 they reach past the texture.

DeviceOptions::render_store_alignment (None by default, as before) names
that reach. Under Alias a padded target is then an image over its rows only
where the stores stay inside its own rows (stores_stay_in_rows): one slice,
its height a multiple of the aligned height, its rows at least its aligned
width apart, and the last row's aligned bytes inside the buffer; another
stays a shadow.

pitched_surfaces::a_store_alignment_keeps_the_padded_targets_its_stores_would_overrun_shadows:
under 16 x 4 each padded layout is aliased exactly where it is without the
alignment and fits (lavapipe: 1307x512/5248, 300x200/1216 and 1913x96/7680
kept, 657x128/5312 RGBA16Float made a shadow). The pitched_surfaces tests
(22, run without the validation layer, which WSL lacks) pass.
